{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":95356,"duration_api_ms":166889,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"571db5c5-415f-48f8-91b3-978273d4cda3","total_cost_usd":0.5149446000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":29585,"cache_read_input_tokens":84301,"output_tokens":3306,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":29585,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":138,"outputTokens":7980,"cacheReadInputTokens":434611,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97375,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.20521785000000003,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3306,"cacheReadInputTokens":84301,"cacheCreationInputTokens":29585,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.30972675000000005,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all seven amendments against the codebase. Five amendments identify real, verified issues: the legacy migration valid_range mismatch, the unannotated kinetic rate parameters, the uncommented ATMOSPHERIC_CO2_PPM constant, the bead delivery gap, and the meq/mg unit-safety problem. Two amendments propose marginal improvements that would duplicate provenance information already maintained in authoritative locations or set an unrealistic coverage bar for the current bead scope.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-92da51e1","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: move_legacy_process_param_meta_key() at presets.rs:2228-2239 copies metadata verbatim via or_insert(legacy_value), while legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l() divides the actual parameter value by LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L (20.0). This means valid_range bounds remain in whole-tank-total scale while the parameter itself is now in mg/L concentration scale — a factor-of-20 mismatch that would cause range validation to silently pass or fail incorrectly."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-c9b5f0d8","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment overstates the bead's coverage requirements. process/default.toml has 20+ annotated parameters, hard_shrimp.toml is fully annotated, and the substrate files have colonizable_area_factor annotated. PROVENANCE_STATUS.md explicitly documents the remaining files as deferred follow-up. Demanding per-parameter entries in every preset file goes beyond what 'representative enriched files' requires — the pattern is already demonstrated across chemistry, ecology, and shrimp tracks."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-1a29bd8c","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified that low_temp_repro_ramp_width_c is already marked placeholder in neocaridina_davidi.toml (lines 130-139) with explicit notes that it lacks literature support, and in PROVENANCE_STATUS.md (line 136). Adding a duplicative TODO at the single usage site in shrimp.rs:1584 creates another location where provenance state must be maintained. The authoritative metadata is already in the right place — the TOML param_meta and provenance docs. Runtime validation (if needed) should check param_meta programmatically, not rely on code comments."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f497e356","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: process/default.toml annotates all K_s half-saturation constants with param_meta but has zero annotations for any vmax, growth_yield, or decay_rate parameter across AOB, NOB, comammox, and decomposer guilds. These rate/yield constants are equally load-bearing for cycling speed and biomass dynamics. Without confidence annotations, downstream calibration work cannot distinguish literature-backed values from tuning knobs, which is exactly the problem the provenance system is designed to solve."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-7fd25e44","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: ATMOSPHERIC_CO2_PPM at chemistry.rs:17 is set to 410.0 with only the comment 'Atmospheric CO2 concentration in ppm.' The nearby provenance block (lines 7-14) discusses the general approach but doesn't cite a source for this specific value. Since it feeds every Henry's law equilibrium calculation, a one-line source note (e.g., NOAA global average circa 2020, treated as fixed for current model scope) is a minimal and warranted improvement for scientific reproducibility."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-2eb078b6","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the worktree changes at tanksim-6e5.4.7 consist of alkalinity-budget plumbing in nitrogen_cycle.rs (alkalinity consumption tracking), water_change.rs (alkalinity exchange), and budget.rs (BudgetDelta with alkalinity field). While the worktree does contain provenance infrastructure (provenance.rs module with ParamMeta, ConfidenceLevel, etc.), no priority parameter families were actually annotated with provenance metadata, and no developer-facing provenance summary was added. If this patch represents bead 6e5.7.2, its acceptance criteria remain unmet."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-7fcbfd69","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified thoroughly: ElementBudget fields are named in_mg/out_mg/net_mg, but the alkalinity field in BudgetDelta stores meq values in these mg-named fields. The code acknowledges this with comments ('Alkalinity in meq (not mg). The field names in_mg/out_mg on ElementBudget are reused even though the unit is meq') and special-cases the unit string in assertion logic. This is a real unit-safety problem — the type system provides no protection against mixing mg and meq values, and the comment-based guardrails will not scale as more systems produce alkalinity budget entries."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"955234a4-4c82-4824-920a-9b2765715801"}
